# Fast smoke gate, not a mirror of CI.
#
# Every push and PR runs the full matrix: `pnpm check`, `pnpm test` and
# `pnpm build` on three OSes, `cargo fmt`/`clippy`/`test` on three OSes,
# prettier, and the browser e2e suite. Re-running all of that locally cost
# ~200s per push (build alone was 109s of it) to learn what CI reports
# anyway a few minutes later. Pushing nine branches took half an hour.
#
# What stays is the pair with the best signal per second: a type error or a
# failing unit test is the overwhelmingly common way a push is broken, and
# catching them here costs ~70s instead of a CI round trip.
#
# What was dropped, and why it is safe:
#   pnpm build        109s, and the js CI job builds on all three OSes. A
#                     failure that `check` and `test` both miss is rare.
#   pnpm format:check pre-commit already runs prettier over staged files via
#                     lint-staged, and the format CI job covers the rest.
#   pnpm lint:theme   moved into the format CI job — it was enforced *only*
#                     here, which meant --no-verify or a fresh clone skipped
#                     it entirely.
#   cargo test        the rust CI job runs it on three OSes. Cheap warm (~7s)
#                     but a cold rebuild after a branch switch dominated
#                     everything else here.
#
# Use `git push --no-verify` when you deliberately want CI to be the first
# thing that runs, e.g. pushing a WIP branch for a second pair of eyes.
pnpm check
pnpm test
